 | NON-SHRINK GROUT
 | Single-Component Non-Shrinking Cementitious Grout
 | TECHNICAL DATA SHEET VER NO. N.1
PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS
Trubuild Non-Shrink Grout is single-component cementitious grout, which can withstand static and dynamic loads. It is
having cement, graded ﬁllers and chemical additives which impart controlled expansion in the plastic state & minimises water
demand. It is suitable for the grouting works of gap thickness from 10 mm to 100 mm.
 | FEATURES & ADVANTAGES
 | NON-SHRINK | HIGH COMPRESSIVE | GOOD FLOW | NON-CORROSIVE
 | STRENGTH
 | Chloride free.
 | Ready-to-use cement mix and requiring the simple addition of water.
 | Indoor & Outdoor
AREAS OF APPLICATION | PACKAGING
 | 20 kg
 • Typical applications would be the grouting of base plates of turbines,
 compressors, boiler feed pumps, etc. • It can also be used for anchoring a
 wide range of ﬁxings.These include anchor bolts and fence posts.
METHOD OF APPLICATION
SURFACE PREPARATION
Ÿ | Concrete surface should be clean, sound and free from oil, grease, laitance and loosely adhering particles.
Ÿ | Metal surface should be free from scale, rust, oil and grease.
Ÿ | All adsorbent surfaces must be well soaked with clean water.
CURING
Allow 28 days curing for full strength. Good curing practice is essential for all exposed surfaces: curing using water.
MIXING
Mixing ratio for desired consistency is as follows.
 S.No. | CONSISTENCY | WATER (L) PER 20 KG BAG
 | 01. | FLOWABLE | 3.8
  02. | POURABLE | 3.2
  03. | STIFF | 2.8
--- PAGE 2 ---
NON SHRINK GROUT HS
 | TECHNICAL DATA SHEET
 | VER NO. N.1
  Ÿ | Take 75% of water as per desired consistency ﬁrst and then add Trubuild Non-Shrink Grout HS gradually with continuous
 | mixing using a spiral mechanical mixture machine.
  Ÿ | Add remaining water with continuous mixing until desired consistency is not obtained. After mixing, leave for 3-5 minutes
 | to remove entrapped air.
  POURING
  Ÿ | To carry out the pouring work, the mix is poured immediately into the designed frame work. For baseplate grouting un-
 | interrupted ﬂow is required.
  Ÿ | For larger section, it is necessary to mix 1 part of 10 mm silt free aggregates to minimise temperature rise. Other
 | precautions such as the use of chilled water, insulation of the framework or base plate may be required.
